<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for Retribution Paladin DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Icecrown Citadel. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Retribution Paladin Phase 4</h2>
<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit - Aim for 8% Hit%, 263 rating, because all of your abilities are under some form of hit requirement.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise - after this point your expertise is the next thing to keep an eye on.  With our 2p T10, interactions with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50706/tiny-abomination-in-a-jar">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_alchemy_enchantedvial.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tiny Abomination in a Jar</span></a> and <a class="q5 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49623/shadowmourne">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_113.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shadowmourne</span></a>, its very important for all your buttons to hit.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Strength out the wazzoo - Everything you have scales with both ap and spell power, and strength gives you the most bang for your buck for that.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Crit /<wbr/> Agi - Your next prio stat, this is very strong as many of your abilities will proc <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=53382/righteous-vengeance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_righteousvengeance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Righteous Vengeance</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - This is still decent but not nearly as good as it was in TBC.  This will have some issues where <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48801/exorcism">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_excorcism_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Exorcism</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48819/consecration">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_innerfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Consecration</span></a> will have their GCD reduced, which will cause weird stutters in your rotation.  These shouldn't be a major concern but its something to note.</div></li></ol>
<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="tiny-abom-in-a-jar">Tiny Abomination in a Jar for Retribution Paladin Phase 4</h2>With the introduction of P4, we have a new trinket that finally replaces DMCG called <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50706/tiny-abomination-in-a-jar">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_alchemy_enchantedvial.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tiny Abomination in a Jar</span></a>.  This trinket is probably the most important piece of gear you can get for ret in p4, the difference between a ret with and without can be upwards of 2k dps depending on the boss.  The proc gets released after 7/<wbr/>8(264 trinket) stacks, causing a strike with your weapon and proccing a seal strike.  <br/>
<br/>So what this all means is this: Every single auto attack, CS /<wbr/> DS Strike has up to 3 proc chances for jar.  A single Divine Storm can actually instantly proc jar.<br/>
<br/>CONFIRMED NOT TO PROC AS OF SEP 25 PTR:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">seal of command damage</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">vindication</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">heart of the crusader</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">hand of reckoning</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">TAJ cannot proc itself</div></li></ol>
<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="shadowmourne">Shadowmourne</h2>As of right now we do not have any data about how Shadowmourne procs with ret.  When we get this information, we will update this section.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="p4-bis-sets">Phase 4 BIS sets</h2>For phase 4, I'm presenting two primary sets to go for.  Two absolute BIS setups, these are unique between Horde and Alliance, and then one setup that is 200-250 dps behind, but will be much easier to get.  It should be noted, the "lower priority set" can run without the SOV glyph, and  These sets are:<div class="clear"></div>
