<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="tier-9-and-tier-10">Tier 9 and Tier 10</h3>Ret Tier 10 is probably one of the most fun tier bonuses made to date in classic, giving you the ability to continously spam <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=53385/divine-storm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_divinestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Divine Storm</span></a> after auto attack refreshes.  When you are progressing in ICC, you want to immediately get to 2p tier 10 as soon as possible.  Even if you don't have any tokens to update these to 264 &amp; 277, you want to instantly get yourself to 2p T10.  Ideally you want to keep 2 pieces of 258 until you have AT LEAST one extra token for 4pieces of T10, meaning you should have your 2p T9 258 pieces replaced with at least one 264 T10 rather than two 251 pieces.  It will be better to upgrade your T10 2p slots as well.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems-of-frost">Emblems of Frost for Retribution Paladin Phase 4</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> has multiple acquisition methods, you can get ~100 per week depending on how diligent you are with your daily activities.  <br/>
<br/>With these numbers in mind you need to plan your upgrades correctly: <br/>You want to simply get all of your tier, ideally all 5 slots, initially.  You should hold off until after you do VOA week 2 to even spend on them to see what you get there.  This will cost 60 for shoulder /<wbr/> gloves, and then 95 for chest /<wbr/> helm /<wbr/> pants, costing 405 in total.  After that, you should look at getting <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50455/libram-of-three-truths">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scroll_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Libram of Three Truths</span></a>, which gives you 20 total more strength than the P3 libram, but is also not limited to SOV if you need to cleave some dudes. After that, I cannot honestly recommend any other item from the emblem of frost market, so you're best bet is to start investing in <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49908/primordial-saronite">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_felflamebreath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Primordial Saronite</span></a>.  <br/>
<br/>
