<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="p3-gear-for-p4">Strong P3 gear for going into P4</h3>Realistically in P4, the only item you're going to carry over is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47464/deaths-choice">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Choice</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47131/deaths-verdict">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Verdict</span></a>.  The damage delta between this and a 245 version of the trinket is about 100dps, but the 245 trinket is still better than just about anything you can get otherwise. After that theres a few items that can last you until you get some 277 replacements, but as a whole there are 0 things that you're going to run long term and will replace most all things even with 264s if you are going to spend some time with normal modes.  I'm honestly not going to list these because they just aren't relevant enough.  You will probably run your 2p T9 until about week 4 of P4 simply because you're just waiting on badges.  It should also be noted that a few sets out there have found <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47473/greaves-of-the-saronite-citadel">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Greaves of the Saronite Citadel</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47154/greaves-of-the-7th-legion">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Greaves of the 7th Legion</span></a> to be effective in a lower priority set, so it may be worth to try and have these before phase ends, or try to snag this if you're going back for a 258 trinket.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="gemming">Gemming your Gear</h3>When gemming your gear you want to keep in mind a few basic notes:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Jewelcrafting is BIS for you, but by only 2 total strength when compared to blacksmithing .  This will give you a bonus of 42 to what ever stats you gem, where as blacksmithing will give you only 40.  With this you will want to make sure you are always running 3 <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42225/dragons-eye">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dragon's Eye</span></a> gems.  These can be purchased with your <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=61/dalaran-jewelcrafters-token">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_variety_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dalaran Jewelcrafter's Token</span></span></a>.  Ideally these should all be <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42142/bold-dragons-eye">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bold Dragon's Eye</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Never be afraid to gem for hit. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42156/rigid-dragons-eye">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid Dragon's Eye</span></a> will provide about 1% hit, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40125/rigid-kings-amber">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_38.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid King's Amber</span></a> provides about .61% hit, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40143/etched-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Etched Ametrine</span></a> will provide ~.3% hit.  These are great ways to make up for a few points missing in a great gear setup otherwise, and are used in the P4 Horde BIS setup.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Because you want to be running <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=41398/relentless-earthsiege-diamond">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_shadowspirit_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relentless Earthsiege Diamond</span></a>, you will only ever need one blue gem, which you should supply by using a single <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49110/nightmare-tear">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_pearl_12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nightmare Tear</span></a>.  This gem provides more overall stats than any purple gem you could use.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Almost all other gems will be <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40111/bold-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bold Cardinal Ruby</span></a>.  The only time you should deviate from this after hit cap is if you can get a yellow socket with 4 strength per yellow socket bonus.  If that's the case you can fill it with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40142/inscribed-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Ametrine</span></a>. This <i>may</i> appear to sim slightly lower than just str, but it will improve your overall consistency going into this phase.</div></li></ol>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="gearing-in-icc">Gearing in ICC</h3>With Wrath, pretty much all your gear minus one trinket will be a 277 item.  In general you can safely assume that the 277 item will be better than a 264 version of an item<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="body-armor">Body Armor for Retribution Paladin Phase 4</h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="head">Head for Retribution Paladin Phase 4</h3>You're going to be running <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51277/sanctified-lightsworn-helmet">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_154.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sanctified Lightsworn Helmet</span></a> for helm slot.  Since you want 4p, and the stats on this are just perfect, theres no reason to not run this.  There are quite a few helm options, but with the power of the 2/<wbr/>4p of Tier10, and the fact the tier pieces are honestly quite easy to acquire, this should be your only option that you aim for.  <br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Helm Enchant</b>: <a class="q7 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50367/arcanum-of-torment">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_rampage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of Torment</span></a>, requires Revered reputation with <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/faction=1098/knights-of-the-ebon-blade">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Knights of the Ebon Blade</span></a>.<div class="pad"></div>
